@1 = ~Ah, Alyth. A lady whose beauty matches only her soul. I remember spending some time with her. Nothing too extraordinary, just a couple of adults committing to a deep... conversation.~
@2 = ~Hah. Coran, we all know exactly what your deep 'conversations' entail.~
@3 = ~Don't live in jealousy, Safana. As precious as her company was, yours is much more desirable.~
@4 = ~Have no fear. We will cause no trouble.~
@5 = ~Yet another dreadful place screaming our name. It's almost as if people want us to die.~
@6 = ~Irrecusable offer indeed.~
@7 = ~You too, sir.~
@8 = ~If only we could do much more for this region than that.~
@9 = ~Watch your foul mouth, stinky! We are far more civilised than your insult of a race.~
@10 = ~Clangeddin, grant me strength. Can't we none of us just go our separate ways in peace? 'Tis all I ask.~
@11 = ~I apologise for having an opinion. I mean no harm. Go ahead.~
@12 = ~Balgrim. That how you greet an old friend, you lousy bastard?~
@13 = ~Kagain! I didn't recognise ya! How's life treating ya? New mercenaries?~
@14 = ~These are my henchmen. Could use some more sturdiness, maybe fix their posture... ahem, possibly work on their attitude, but you know what it is nowadays.~
@15 = ~Sure do. Well, I ain't botherin' ya any longer. Keep training your obedient doggies.~
@16 = ~Will do.~
@17 = ~What a platonic friendship. Gossiping about partners, friendly insults. You two remind me of me and <CHARNAME> a lot.~
@18 = ~Lass, life of a mercenary spares no time for friendships. I focus on money, business and merchandise. Your little lovey-dovey affiliation with our so fearless leader is irrelevant. My relationships are strictly transactional in nature.~
@19 = ~How far can you potentially get in life without having someone who can lend you a hand if needed? You see, without friendship...~
@20 = ~Lass! I have no time or intention to listen to it. If I gave you a lecture on how to abolish your funny idea of friendship with enterprise, would you listen?~
@21 = ~Well, probably not. But I...~
@22 = ~There's your answer.~
@23 = ~An invaluable trait of being a woman is impatience. Waiting gains you nothing. Taking immediately will make you a very wealthy girl when you grow up.~
